Section 12. All applicants for registration as master plumber shall be required to pass an examination as hereinafter provided.
Persons applying for admission to the examination as herein provided, shall, prior to the date of the examination, establish to the satisfaction of the Board of Examiners, that he:
(a) Is at least twenty-one years of age;
(b) Is a citizen of the Philippines;
(c) Is of good moral character;
(d) Is at least a high school graduate;
(e) Has at least five years experience in actual plumbing work under the supervision of a registered master plumber.

Section 13. Applicants for registration as master plumbers shall be examined in the following subjects:
(a) Plumbing arithmetic, ten per cent;
(b) Plumbing Code, ten per cent;
(c) Sanitation, plumbing design and installation, forty per cent;
(d) Practical problems, twenty per cent;
(e) Oral practical problems and experience, twenty per cent.
